# Environment
#
# `.env` IS TRACKED on purpose — it holds the shared Supabase project URL and
# anon key so a teammate can clone and run with no setup. Both are public by
# design: the anon key ships in browser JavaScript on every deploy, and
# row-level security is what protects the data, not the key's secrecy.
#
# EVERY ACTUAL SECRET GOES IN .env.local, which is ignored below. Anything with
# "key", "secret", or "token" in the name that is NOT the Supabase anon key
# belongs there — ANTHROPIC_API_KEY especially, and the Supabase service_role
# key, which bypasses RLS entirely and must never be committed.
.env.local
.env.development.local
.env.test.local
.env.production.local
.env*.local

